Relevant columns and their usage  

• posts_questions.id : question id, needed to link to answers  
• posts_questions.body : the text we measure (LENGTH(body))  
• posts_questions.accepted_answer_id : used to know whether the question has an accepted answer  
• posts_questions.view_count : denominator for the score‑to‑view ratio  
• posts_questions.owner_user_id : links the question to the author  

• posts_answers.parent_id : links answers to their question  
• posts_answers.score : numerator for the score‑to‑view ratio  

• users.id : joins to owner_user_id  
• users.reputation : requested in result  
• users.up_votes / users.down_votes : to compute net votes (up‑down)  

• badges.user_id : joins to users to count the number of badges a user has earned  

Conditions that will be needed  

1. LENGTH(q.body) – to sort by body length  
2. q.accepted_answer_id IS NOT NULL   OR  
   (q.accepted_answer_id IS NULL AND  
    EXISTS a with SAFE_DIVIDE(a.score , q.view_count) > 0.01)  

Below are ten progressively richer exploratory SQL statements (all capped with LIMIT 20) that build up to the final answer.

```sql
-- 1) Look at some of the raw question rows
SELECT id, body, accepted_answer_id, view_count, owner_user_id
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Compute the length of the body for a sample of questions
SELECT id,
       LENGTH(body) AS body_length,
       accepted_answer_id
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
ORDER BY body_length DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Only questions that already have an accepted answer
SELECT id,
       LENGTH(body) AS body_length,
       accepted_answer_id
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE accepted_answer_id IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY body_length DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Join one answer per question to see answer scores and compute the ratio
SELECT q.id AS question_id,
       a.id AS answer_id,
       a.score,
       q.view_count,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(a.score, NULLIF(q.view_count,0)) AS score_view_ratio
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`  AS q
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`    AS a
  ON a.parent_id = q.id
WHERE q.view_count IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Keep only answers whose score‑to‑view ratio is higher than 0.01
SELECT q.id AS question_id,
       a.id AS answer_id,
       SAFE_DIVIDE(a.score, NULLIF(q.view_count,0)) AS score_view_ratio
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`  AS q
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`    AS a
  ON a.parent_id = q.id
WHERE SAFE_DIVIDE(a.score, NULLIF(q.view_count,0)) > 0.01
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Questions that (1) have no accepted answer but (2) satisfy the ratio rule
SELECT DISTINCT q.id
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`  AS q
WHERE q.accepted_answer_id IS NULL
  AND EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers` AS a
        WHERE a.parent_id = q.id
          AND SAFE_DIVIDE(a.score, NULLIF(q.view_count,0)) > 0.01
      )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Union of (A) questions with accepted answers OR (B) those that pass the ratio rule
SELECT DISTINCT q.id
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`  AS q
WHERE q.accepted_answer_id IS NOT NULL
   OR (
        q.accepted_answer_id IS NULL
        AND EXISTS (
              SELECT 1
              FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers` AS a
              WHERE a.parent_id = q.id
                AND SAFE_DIVIDE(a.score, NULLIF(q.view_count,0)) > 0.01
            )
      )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Add user information (reputation and net votes)
SELECT q.id                     AS question_id,
       u.id                     AS user_id,
       u.reputation,
       (u.up_votes - u.down_votes) AS net_votes
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.users`           AS u
  ON u.id = q.owner_user_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Add badge counts per user
WITH badge_count AS (
  SELECT user_id, COUNT(*) AS badge_total
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.badges`
  GROUP BY user_id
)
SELECT u.id AS user_id,
       u.reputation,
       (u.up_votes - u.down_votes) AS net_votes,
       bc.badge_total
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.users` AS u
LEFT JOIN badge_count AS bc
  ON bc.user_id = u.id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Final query – the 20 longest questions that satisfy the accepted‑answer / ratio rule,
--      with asker reputation, net votes, and badge count
WITH badge_count AS (
  SELECT user_id, COUNT(*) AS badge_total
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.badges`
  GROUP BY user_id
)
SELECT
  q.id                               AS question_id,
  LENGTH(q.body)                     AS body_length,
  q.accepted_answer_id,
  u.reputation,
  (u.up_votes - u.down_votes)        AS net_votes,
  COALESCE(bc.badge_total,0)         AS badge_total
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.users`           AS u
  ON u.id = q.owner_user_id
LEFT JOIN badge_count AS bc
  ON bc.user_id = u.id
WHERE
  ( q.accepted_answer_id IS NOT NULL )
  OR
  ( q.accepted_answer_id IS NULL
    AND EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers` AS a
        WHERE a.parent_id = q.id
          AND SAFE_DIVIDE(a.score, NULLIF(q.view_count,0)) > 0.01
      )
  )
ORDER BY body_length DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

